<title>JORDAN: Jordanian trade gap widens by 68 pct in March.</title>
<headline>Jordanian trade gap widens by 68 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jordan's March trade deficit grew by 68 percent to 176.97 million dinars ($250 million) from 105.53 million dinars in February, the Central Bank bulletin said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Imports rose by 100 million dinars to 285 million dinars. Consumer goods imports nearly doubled to 66.3 million dinars from 34.5 million, while capital goods imports also rose sharply to 47.3 million dinars from 25.9 million.</p>
<p>The March deficit was 29 percent greater than the same month last year.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of dinars)</p>
<p>			 March 97   Feb 97   Mar 96    1996     1995</p>
<p> Domestic exports  88.68	64.43    79.81     1,039    1,004</p>
<p> Re-exports	  19.45	16.01    22.30     248	237</p>
<p> Imports	     285.10     185.97   239.75    3,043    2,590</p>
<p> Trade balance     -176.97    -105.53  -137.64   -1,756   -1,349</p>
<p>$1 = 0.709 dinars</p>
<p>--Amman newsroom 9626 623 776</p>
